# Check every text file out with LF on every platform. Git for Windows
# defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite line endings in the
# working tree; several checks compare bytes against a file on disk — the
# IANA table generator's -check mode renders LF and compares it to
# go/policy_iana.go, and the conformance/IANA drift tests byte-compare their
# testdata mirrors — so a CRLF checkout fails them for a difference that does
# not exist in the repository. Nothing here is committed with CRLF, so this
# changes checkout behavior only.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Go fuzz corpus files are byte-exact test inputs; CRLF conversion on
# Windows checkouts would corrupt them. Listed last so it wins over the
# blanket rule above.
go/testdata/fuzz/** -text
